      <h3 class="pq-routes-heading">Inside the API</h3>
      <p class="pq-routes-sub">60 routes, grouped by what they actually do &mdash; moderation and admin routes are covered below.</p>
      <div class="pq-routes-list">
        <div class="pq-routes-row">
          <span class="pq-routes-label">Parks &amp; maps</span>
          <span class="pq-routes-desc">Proxies live NPS data, per-park weather, and who else has visited.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pq-routes-row">
          <span class="pq-routes-label">Visits &amp; hikes</span>
          <span class="pq-routes-desc">Logs trips and bucket-list entries; parses GPX uploads into distance, elevation, and route.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pq-routes-row">
          <span class="pq-routes-label">Social feed</span>
          <span class="pq-routes-desc">Posts, likes, comments, quote/reposts, and badge-share posts.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pq-routes-row">
          <span class="pq-routes-label">Friends</span>
          <span class="pq-routes-desc">Mutual request/accept model &mdash; not a one-way follow.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pq-routes-row">
          <span class="pq-routes-label">Badges</span>
          <span class="pq-routes-desc">Awards and revokes badges through one shared condition engine.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pq-routes-row">
          <span class="pq-routes-label">Notifications</span>
          <span class="pq-routes-desc">One typed feed, fanned out to Web Push and Expo push in parallel.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pq-routes-row">
          <span class="pq-routes-label">Auth &amp; webhooks</span>
          <span class="pq-routes-desc">Clerk's <code>user.created</code> webhook backstops profile creation for SSO signups.</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ul class="pq-notes">
        <li>One Next.js backend serves both clients &mdash; 60 API routes shared by the iOS app and the web app, kept in sync by <code>@parkquest/types</code>, a package of shared domain types (parks, visits, social, moderation, badges) both apps import as the API contract.</li>
        <li>That package also ships shared SVG glyph geometry for the passport stamps (<code>parkGlyphs.ts</code>) &mdash; web's <code>Stamp</code> component and iOS's <code>ParkStamp</code> render pixel-identical stamp art from the same <code>glyphTransform()</code> function, not duplicated per platform.</li>
        <li>Badges are entirely data-driven: every badge, including the launch set, is a database row evaluated by a condition engine, not a hardcoded list.</li>
        <li>The web app renders its own MapLibre GL vector map; iOS uses react-native-maps with <code>PROVIDER_DEFAULT</code>, which resolves to Apple MapKit rather than Google Maps. GPX uploads power real hike stats (distance, elevation, route) without a third-party fitness integration.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="pq-routes-heading">Admin &amp; moderation</h3>
      <p class="pq-routes-sub">A private dashboard, not linked anywhere else on this page &mdash; <code>/admin</code>, gated by <code>requireAdmin()</code>. Here's what's actually behind it.</p>

      <div class="pq-admin-feature">
        <h4>Reconciling Apple's App Store Connect reporting</h4>
        <p>A daily Vercel Cron job merges Apple's two separate, laggy reporting pipelines into one metrics table.</p>
        <ul class="pq-notes">
          <li>Pulls the Sales Reports API (units, proceeds) and the Analytics Reports API (impressions, page views, downloads vs. redownloads) &mdash; two report families, different formats, different lag.</li>
          <li>Re-walks a trailing 7 days, not just yesterday, since Apple's reports land 24&ndash;48h late and inconsistently &mdash; one run both catches new days and repairs partial ones.</li>
          <li>Auth is hand-rolled: an ES256 JWT signed with Apple's <code>.p8</code> key via Node's <code>crypto</code> directly, no JWT library &mdash; App Store Connect tokens cap at 20 minutes.</li>
          <li>Idempotent, per-column upserts &mdash; a sales-only run can't clobber an analytics-only run, and an unpublished day shows as a gap on the charts, not a fake zero.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="pq-routes-list pq-admin-list">
        <div class="pq-routes-row">
          <span class="pq-routes-label">Dashboard</span>
          <span class="pq-routes-desc">Live signups, DAU, active-user windows, top parks by visits.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pq-routes-row">
          <span class="pq-routes-label">Moderation</span>
          <span class="pq-routes-desc">Review queue for user reports and blocks.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pq-routes-row">
          <span class="pq-routes-label">Badges</span>
          <span class="pq-routes-desc">CRUD manager for the condition-engine badges.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pq-routes-row">
