       viewBox on either end — pixel-scanning the rendered trace found a
       ~1% margin at the top and ~1.2% at the bottom before the frame art
       actually starts/stops. Content can't cross either or it shows
       through the transparent margin, past the frame entirely, against
       the page background — not miscropped, genuinely outside the phone. */
    top: 2.2%;
    /* Widened past the 4.1% that exactly matches content aspect at the
       original top+bottom budget (2.6%) — more margin on both edges needs
       more combined budget (now 4%), and the only way to keep the same
       0.461 content aspect at a bigger budget is a narrower box. */
    left: 4.8%;
    right: 4.8%;
    bottom: 1.8%;
    /* Rounded well past what the frame's own curve strictly needs, on
       purpose — the bezel is a hand trace, not a perfect arc, and erring
